Algorithm: Campus Wi-Fi Network Using Adjacency Matrix with Modifications

Step 1: Start.
Step 2: Input the number of Wi-Fi access points n and their names.
Step 3: Create an n*n adjacency matrix and initialize all elements to 0.
Step 4: Input the number of direct network links (e).
Step 5: For each edge, input two vertex indices (u) and (v). Validate the indices and set adj[u-1][v-1] = 1 and adj[v-1][u-1] = 
Step 6: Display the menu with the following operations:
          1. Display graph
          2. Insert a new vertex and its edges
          3. Remove a selected edge
          4. Display degree and direct neighbours
          5. Exit
Step 7: Accept the user's choice.

A. Insertion of a New Vertex
Step 8: If the user selects choice 2, input the name of the new access point.
Step 9: Expand the adjacency matrix by adding one row and one column initialized to 0.
Step 10: Input the number of edges for the new vertex and the indices of the existing vertices to connect.
Step 11: Update the corresponding matrix entries to 1 in both directions and display the updated adjacency matrix.

B. Deletion of a Selected Edge
Step 12: If the user selects choice 3, input the indices of the two vertices whose edge is to be removed.
Step 13: Check whether the indices are valid and the edge exists.
Step 14: If valid, set adj[u-1][v-1] = 0 and adj[v-1][u-1] = 0. Otherwise, display an error message.
Step 15: Display the updated adjacency matrix.

C. Calculation of Degree and Direct Neighbours
Step 16: If the user selects choice 4, input the index of the vertex to be checked.
Step 17: Validate the vertex index.
Step 18: Traverse the corresponding row of the adjacency matrix. Display the names of all vertices connected to the selected vertex and count the connections.
Step 19: Display the degree of the selected vertex and its direct neighbours.

Menu Control
Step 20: If the user selects choice 1, display the current adjacency matrix.
Step 21: If the user selects choice 5, terminate the program.
Step 22: For any other choice, display an invalid-choice message.
Step 23: Repeat the menu until the user selects Exit.
Step 24: Stop.
